# Ureni, the Song Unending: the targets and their shares are fixed as the trigger goes on the stack (CR 601.2d), and a target that is gone
# by the time it resolves is taken out with its share (CR 608.2b), the damage is not given to another. Bot1 has two lands on turn 5, so X is
# 2 and is divided 1 to Bot2's Memnite and 1 to its Ornithopter (0/2); in response Bot1's Lightning Bolt (Mox Ruby) kills the Memnite, and the
# Ornithopter still takes only its own 1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Ruby
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Lightning Bolt
Ureni, the Song Unending
Forest
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ureni, the Song Unending.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Divide(Memnite: 1; Ornithopter: 1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Memnite)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Graveyard = Memnite
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Memnite
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Damage = 1
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt; Black Lotus
